The review has been written to `docs/reviews/hpxml/hpxml-05-refrigerator-location-string-match.md`.

Summary: 3 findings — 1 high, 1 medium, 1 low. The core issue is that `is_conditioned_location()` at `resolve_loads.rs:754` uses exact string matching on only 3 strings, while the codebase already has `parse_zone_label()` in `building.rs:2347` that does proper keyword-based classification. This causes refrigerators in conditions like "basement - conditioned" to silently get zeroed gains.
